ber of legs is \\( 51 \\) more than the number of goats. How many goats are there?","options":["\\( 16 \\)","\\( 17 \\)","\\( 18 \\)","\\( 19 \\)","\\( 20 \\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 4g - g = 51 \\Rightarrow 3g = 51 \\Rightarrow g = 17 \\)."],"hint":"If there are \\( g \\) goats, \\( 4g = g + 51 \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which of the following fractions is the greatest?","options":["\\( \\dfrac{11}{12} \\)","\\( \\dfrac{13}{14} \\)","\\( \\dfrac{15}{16} \\)","\\( \\dfrac{17}{18} \\)","\\( \\dfrac{19}{20} \\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( \\frac{19}{20} = 1-\\frac{1}{20} \\) has the smallest gap, so it is the largest."],"hint":"Each is \\( 1 \\) minus a small fraction; the smallest gap wins.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the square of \\( 5^2 \\).","options":["\\( 5 \\)","\\( 125 \\)","\\( 250 \\)","\\( 475 \\)","\\( 625 \\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( (5^2)^2 = 25^2 = 625 \\)."],"hint":"\\( 5^2 = 25 \\); now square that.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"An ‘interesting number’ is the product of two prime numbers. Which of the following is NOT interesting?","options":["\\( 6 \\)","\\( 10 \\)","\\( 12 \\)","\\( 14 \\)","\\( 15 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 6=2\\times3,10=2\\times5,14=2\\times7,15=3\\times5 \\); but \\( 12=2\\times2\\times3 \\) needs three primes."],"hint":"Factorise each into primes.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The sum of the first \\( n \\) odd numbers is \\( n^2 \\). Evaluate \\( 1+3+5+\\cdots+29 \\).","options":["\\( 169 \\)","\\( 196 \\)","\\( 225 \\)","\\( 256 \\)","\\( 289 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 29 = 2(15)-1 \\), so there are \\( 15 \\) terms: \\( 15^2 = 225 \\)."],"hint":"How many odd numbers up to \\( 29 \\)?","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find \\( \\sqrt{4} \\).","options":["\\( 1 \\)","\\( 2 \\)","\\( 4 \\)","\\( 8 \\)","\\( 16 \\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 2\\times 2 = 4 \\), so \\( \\sqrt{4} = 2 \\)."],"hint":"What number times itself is \\( 4 \\)?","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find \\( x \\) if \\( 3 : 2x = 12 : 40 \\).","options":["\\( 1 \\)","\\( 2 \\)","\\( 4 \\)","\\( 5 \\)","\\( 8 \\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 120 = 24x \\Rightarrow x = 5 \\)."],"hint":"Cross-multiply: \\( 3\\times 40 = 12\\times 2x \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The sum of two of the numbers \\( -7, -4, -3, -1, 3, 5 \\) is \\( 0 \\). What is the product of these two numbers?","options":["\\( -9 \\)","\\( -6 \\)","\\( -5 \\)","\\( 2 \\)","\\( 12 \\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( -3 + 3 = 0 \\); their product is \\( -3\\times 3 = -9 \\)."],"hint":"Which pair are opposites?","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Evaluate \\( (7a - 5)\\times(3a - 8) \\) when \\( a = 1 \\).","options":["\\( -10 \\)","\\( -8 \\)","\\( -6 \\)","\\( -5 \\)","\\( -2 \\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( (7-5)(3-8) = 2\\times(-5) = -10 \\)."],"hint":"Substitute \\( a=1 \\) first.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"On the number line the interval between \\( 3 \\) and \\( 4 \\) is divided into \\( 5 \\) equal parts, and the value \\( a\\tfrac{b}{5} \\) is marked. What is \\( a+b \\)?","options":["\\( 5 \\)","\\( 6 \\)","\\( 7 \\)","\\( 8 \\)","\\( 9 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["The mark is at \\( 3\\tfrac{4}{5} \\), so \\( a=3,\\,b=4 \\) and \\( a+b = 7 \\). ⚠ Position read from the scan — verify against the official figure."],"hint":"The whole-number part is \\( 3 \\); read the marked fifth.","image":